{% import "v2/macros.njk" as m %}
{% set app = apps | bySlug('weathertw') %}
{% set playUrl = 'https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=' + app.packageName %}
{% set shots = '/assets/images/weathertw/screenshots/shot_20260521_' %}

{{ m.appHero({
  app: app, lang: 'en',
  category: 'Weather & Road Live', tags: ['Android · iOS', 'Free'],
  title: 'Weather Satellite Taiwan',
  lead: "Satellite, radar, temperature and rainfall maps from Taiwan's Central Weather Administration (CWA), each played as a time-lapse. Known on the device as 天氣衛星圖 / Weather Satellite.",
  playUrl: playUrl, appStoreUrl: app.appStoreUrl,
  facts: ['No sign-up', 'No location permission', 'English · Traditional Chinese', 'Dark mode'],
  shots: [
    { src: shots + '160138_framed.webp', w: 720, h: 1505 },
    { src: shots + '160201_framed.webp', w: 720, h: 1505 }
  ]
}) }}

{{ m.facts([
  { num: '18', label: 'Imagery feeds · one menu grid' },
  { num: '15 frames', label: 'Recent imagery looped at about 300 ms per frame' },
  { num: '9', label: 'Satellite views · Infrared, Infrared Tone, Visible × Taiwan, East Asia, Earth' },
  { num: '6', label: 'Radar feeds · map overlay, composite, neighbor, 3 local stations' }
]) }}

{% call m.feat({ eyebrow: 'One screen', title: 'Eighteen scattered feeds,<br>one menu grid',
  shots: [ { src: shots + '160033_framed.webp', alt: 'Main menu — 18 weather imagery tiles in one grid', w: 720, h: 1505 } ] }) %}
  <p>CWA publishes Taiwan's imagery across separate pages, so comparing the same time slice means hopping between them. Weather Satellite Taiwan groups everything onto one menu.</p>
  <ul class="checks">
    <li>Each tile shows the <strong>latest thumbnail</strong> (cached about five minutes) — a read on the sky as soon as it opens</li>
    <li>Every feed <strong>downloads its most recent 15 frames</strong> and plays them at about 300 ms each</li>
    <li>Not a single still — <strong>where the clouds and rain come from and where they go</strong></li>
  </ul>
{% endcall %}

{% call m.feat({ eyebrow: 'Satellite', title: 'Infrared, Infrared Tone, Visible<br>at three ranges', soft: true, flip: true,
  shots: [
    { src: shots + '160118_framed.webp', alt: 'Infrared satellite — Taiwan, cloud distribution with timestamp and playback controls', w: 720, h: 1505 },
    { src: shots + '160138_framed.webp', alt: 'Infrared Tone — Taiwan, strong convective clouds picked out in red and magenta', w: 720, h: 1505 }
  ] }) %}
  <p>Three satellite channels, each at Taiwan / East Asia / Earth coverage. Every feed opens in a fullscreen viewer with the publish timestamp shown at the top.</p>
  <ul class="checks">
    <li><strong>Infrared</strong> — cloud-top temperature in grayscale, works at night</li>
    <li><strong>Infrared Tone</strong> — the coldest, most <strong>convective cloud tops</strong> in red and magenta</li>
    <li><strong>Visible</strong> — daytime imagery close to natural color (dark at night)</li>
  </ul>
{% endcall %}

{% call m.feat({ eyebrow: 'Radar', title: 'Is it raining<br>where I am?',
  shots: [
    { src: shots + '160201_framed.webp', alt: 'Radar Map — Google Maps with rainfall intensity overlay and opacity slider', w: 720, h: 1505 },
    { src: shots + '160213_framed.webp', alt: 'Composite radar — Taiwan-wide rainfall intensity', w: 720, h: 1505 }
  ] }) %}
  <p>Six radar feeds, each shaped for a different reading. Read the macro shape on the composite, find yourself on the map overlay, then zoom into a local station if something nearby looks intense.</p>
  <ul class="checks">
    <li><strong>Radar Map</strong> — rainfall over Google Maps, with an <strong>opacity slider</strong></li>
    <li><strong>Composite</strong> (all of Taiwan) and <strong>neighbor</strong> (East Asia) — catch incoming systems a step earlier</li>
    <li><strong>Three local radars</strong> — 樹林 · 南屯 · 林園, for the fine structure of local storms</li>
  </ul>
{% endcall %}

{% call m.feat({ eyebrow: 'Temperature · Rain', title: 'Temperature now,<br>rain for the next 24 hours', soft: true, flip: true,
  shots: [
    { src: shots + '160246_framed.webp', alt: 'Temperature distribution — Taiwan-wide color map with right-side scale bar', w: 720, h: 1505 },
    { src: shots + '160259_framed.webp', alt: 'Quantitative Precipitation Forecast — next 0–12h and 12–24h, stacked for comparison', w: 720, h: 1505 }
  ] }) %}
  <p>The temperature map colors Taiwan-wide air temperature. The Quantitative Precipitation Forecast (QPF) is a forecast, not an observation, split into two blocks for the next 24 hours.</p>
  <ul class="checks">
    <li>Scale bar of roughly <strong>8–33 °C</strong> — north vs. south, mountain vs. coast at one timestamp</li>
    <li>QPF <strong>0–12 h / 12–24 h</strong> maps stacked for comparison</li>
    <li><strong>Accumulated daily rainfall</strong> — where and how much it rained over the past day</li>
  </ul>
{% endcall %}

{% call m.more('See all features', 'Loop · Zoom · Timestamps · Dark mode · Languages') %}
  <div>
    <h4>Playback and controls</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>Satellite and radar load 15 frames, QPF loads 2–7 — no setup, the play button just works</li>
      <li>Temperature map: recent 7 frames, about 500 ms per frame</li>
      <li>Pinch to zoom or use ⊕ / ⊖; the left-most button toggles fullscreen</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div>
    <h4>Explicit timestamps</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>On top of the timestamp baked into the imagery, the viewer overlays its own ("2026/05/21 14:30")</li>
      <li>You always see the publish moment, even across time zones</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div>
    <h4>Six radar feeds in detail</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>Radar Map (Taiwan) — the current location pin makes "is it raining here?" a single glance</li>
      <li>Radar (Taiwan) — colors run blue → green → yellow → red as intensity rises</li>
      <li>Radar (neighbor) — composite extended to the East Asia region</li>
      <li>Three local radars — single-site feeds for 樹林 (ShuLin), 南屯 (NanTun), 林園 (LinYuan)</li>
      <li>Every radar feed runs the same 15-frame loop as the satellite views</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <div>
    <h4>Display, languages, storage</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>Dark mode follows the system and desaturates menu icons so the imagery stays the focal point</li>
      <li>English (default) and Traditional Chinese (zh-rTW), switched by device locale</li>
      <li>Once cached imagery exceeds 300 files, the app cleans up automatically</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
{% endcall %}

